{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter's Graduation"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Parting Ways with Mates"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe plans for the organization of events."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Promises"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (with <span class=\"italic\">will</span>) to make promises."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can start the sentence with <span class=\"italic\">\"I promise I'll \u2026 \"</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\"I promise to \u2026 \"</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\"I'll \u2026 \"</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can respond to promises with an expression like:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Great, thank you!</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">Alright.</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">OK.</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">That's fine.</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">Sure, that works.</span>  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Anne</span>: I'll keep in touch, I promise. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Jeff</span>: Great, I look forward to that!"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use the Simple Future tense will and modals like <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to talk about a future that is not decided or certain."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use will to make promises. <br>You use may and might to suggest the possibility of something in the future. Often  Might can suggest a smaller possibility that may. However, there is little difference. Might is more usual than may in spoken English."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He<span class=\"strong\">'ll help</span>  you with your  convocation speech later."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">might meet</span> Vanessa tonight."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to promise"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say you will do something; give your word"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I promise the course will be easy. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le13ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use at a school graduation."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to regret"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be sorry you did something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You won't regret taking this course! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le13ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "alumni"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people who went to the school "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many alumni came to the graduation ceremony."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le13ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to enter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to add; to type in "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let me enter my information into your phone.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le13ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blackboard "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "chalkboard; where teachers write in a classroom "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He wrote so much on the blackboard! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le13ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le13ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue catching up with a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say what you were doing/did in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say what you may/might do in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a promise, like to meet for lunch."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a 50-75 word dialogue catching up with a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I did and was doing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about actions and events in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for their information for my phone."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a promise."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le13ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le13ob05re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le13ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Camilla! Are you here for graduation? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Yes! It's nice to see you Peter! Where do we go?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: This might be the way down here.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Oh, look! There's our accounting classroom.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh, man! Remember the first day? It was horrible!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: Yeah. Mr. Philips was all - \u201cI promise you'll  find this interesting\u201d!<br>", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le13ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: \u201cYou won't have a lot of homework!\u201d <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Camilla</span>: \u201cYou'll all be great accountants! You won't regret taking this course!\u201d<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: All lies!  He was so boring!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\"